sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor IA as Account IAM admin
    actor Adm as Installation admin<br/>(deployer creds)
    actor Op as Benchmark author<br/>(operator creds)
    participant CLI as baas CLI
    participant CFG as ~/.baas/config.yaml
    participant AWS as AWS account

    Note over IA,AWS: The whole life of one installation, from an empty account to an empty account.<br/>Commands in brackets are not baas commands — the CLI cannot do them.

    rect rgb(240, 240, 255)
        Note over IA,AWS: 0. One-time IAM
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin deployer-policy [--region] [--for-account]
        CLI->>AWS: sts:GetCallerIdentity (skipped with --for-account)
        CLI-->>Adm: rendered policy JSON on stdout
        Adm->>IA: hand over the JSON
        IA->>AWS: [attach as customer-managed policy]
        opt CI federation wanted
            IA->>AWS: [deploy cf-template-ci.yaml, or reuse the account's GitHub OIDC provider]
        end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over IA,AWS: 1. Install
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin setup [--region] [--aws-profile]<br/>[--use-existing-vpc --vpc-id --subnet-id --sg-id]<br/>[--github-org --github-repo --oidc-provider-arn]
        CLI->>AWS: preflight (SimulatePrincipalPolicy), retained bucket/table check
        CLI->>AWS: CreateStack <prefix>, wait (~1.5 min)
        CLI->>CFG: write prefix, aws.profile, aws.region
        CLI-->>Adm: OperatorRole ARN + "Nobody can assume it yet" + next: build-image
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin build-image
        CLI->>AWS: preflight version, UpdateStack (image params), StartImagePipelineExecution
        CLI->>AWS: wait (~15 min), tag AMI, PutParameter /<prefix>/runner/ami-id, retire previous AMI
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin image
        CLI-->>Adm: version, AMI, parent, built-at, pointer
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 235)
        Note over IA,AWS: 2. Onboard an operator machine
        Op->>AWS: [grant sts:AssumeRole on <prefix>-role-operator -- add role_arn profile to ~/.aws/config]
        Op->>CLI: baas config sync --name baas-<accountId>
        CLI->>AWS: DescribeStacks (proves it exists)
        CLI->>CFG: write prefix
        Op->>CLI: baas config set --operator-profile p [--region] [--instance-type] [--timeout]<br/>[--watchdog-margin] [--git-resolve-project]
        CLI->>CFG: write
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over IA,AWS: 3. Measure (repeatable, see baas-run.mmd)
        Op->>CLI: baas run --benchmark-jar b.jar --project p [--tag k=v]… jmh -- Bench -f 1
        CLI->>AWS: upload, reserve the job item, RunInstances, poll the job item
        CLI-->>Op: job id + result table
        Op->>CLI: baas results [--project p | --all-projects | --job-id id]
        Op->>CLI: baas download <jobId>
        Op->>CLI: baas env diff <jobIdA> <jobIdB>
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
        Note over IA,AWS: 4. Retire
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin teardown [--delete-bucket] [--yes]
        CLI->>AWS: refuse if a runner is pending/running -- DeleteStack, wait -- then retire the image<br/>(pointer, AMI, snapshot, Image Builder records)
        CLI-->>Adm: warns: table retained (bucket too, without --delete-bucket)
        Note over Adm,AWS: Left behind: the results table (always) and the bucket (without --delete-bucket).<br/>Both are deleted by a future teardown, behind a second confirmation, once baas admin export exists
        Adm->>AWS: [aws dynamodb delete-table, to remove the table today]
        Note over CFG: config.yaml still names the prefix: results keeps reading the retained table,<br/>download and env diff fail once the bucket is gone, run stops at the image lookup:<br/>no runner image is published, and nothing was uploaded
    end
